Experimental source-owned startup discovery retirement; not applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006, bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires the existing caller/auth/refusal patches and omp-restricted-startup.patch.
Modules: ModelRegistry::retireStartupDiscovery and public/private discovery callers;
model-provider-discovery::withModelDiscoveryTimeout; model-discovery::withTimeoutSignal;
provider-models/openai-compat shared catalog request; sdk::retireRestrictedStartupCatalog.
Tests: startup-discovery-owner.test.ts and cli-restricted-startup.test.ts, existing
registry/discovery suites and opencode-provider.test.ts. Native controls are dated in
validation: original operations outlive timeouts; retirement joins their actual IO.
Difference: one opt-in owner established at registry construction. It closes public
discovery admission and joins original operations plus their completion observers,
including response bodies, nested timeout races and detached shared catalog requests.
Ordinary discovery timeout behavior remains. At most 4096 owned operation starts.
Mirrored/unknown/repeated identities and unqualified Cursor native transport refuse.
The fixed qualification profile retains its preceding model/configuration identity.
No complete startup inventory, Ready, transport permission, paid execution, signing,
or physical descriptor shutdown is established by this catalog receipt.

